# Reintersect status

{{CODEX_NOTE}}
```bash
node "{{PLUGIN_ROOT}}/dist/reintersect-agent.mjs" status
```

Summarise the report in plain language and relay its `hint` lines as the next
step. If sign-in is missing or the API is unreachable, say clearly that
memories are NOT being created and point at the login skill. Never report an
authentication failure as "no memories found".

In Codex, if capture is paused, relay the resume hint instead of diagnosing missing
hooks. An enabled capture setting does not prove the hooks ran. Inspect only
the current session's `codex-<session_id>.state.json` and `.jsonl` under the
reported data directory's `sessions/` folder (use `CODEX_THREAD_ID` when available).
Confirm a captured user prompt from this session; old sessions are not proof.
If capture is enabled and the prompt is missing, report setup as incomplete and
direct the user to review and trust Reintersect's hooks (`/hooks` in the Codex CLI),
then start a new session. Never infer
successful recall or upload merely from a local capture record; check the current
session's injected context or advanced `flushedRecords` and relevant errors.
